"hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1249,"Maymun ibn Mahran (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: ""I asked Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) whether Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would invite people to feasts. He said: 'It was not the general practice, but once his camel's leg broke, so we slaughtered it. Then he said: ""Gather the people of Madinah."" Nafi' says: ""I said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, on what basis should I invite them? We do not even have bread."" He said: ""O Allah, all praise belongs to You. These are bones and this broth"" — or he said: ""Broth and meat"" — ""whoever wishes may eat and whoever wishes may leave.""'"""
1250,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace and blessings be upon him) was circumcised at the age of eighty, at the place of Qudum, and he circumcised himself."" Imam al-Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""Qudum is not a place; rather it means 'eighty.'"""
1251,"Umm al-Muhajir (may Allah have mercy on her) narrates: ""I was brought as a captive among the slave-girls of Rome, and Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) invited us to Islam. No one accepted Islam except me and one other woman. Then Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Go, circumcise them and purify them.'"""
1252,"Salim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) circumcised me and Nu'aym, and a ram was slaughtered on our behalf. We would take pride in this over the other boys, that a ram had been slaughtered on our behalf."
1253,"It is narrated by Umm 'Alqamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the nieces of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) were circumcised, so it was said to 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): ""Shall we not call someone to amuse them?"" She said: ""Very well."" So a message was sent to 'Adiyy, and he came. When 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, she saw that he was singing and swaying about, and he had a great deal of hair. 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Ugh! Drive out this Satan, drive him out!"""
1254,"It is narrated by Aslam, the freedman of 'Umar (may Allah have mercy on him), that when we came to Syria with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), the chieftain of that place came to him and said: ""O Commander of the Faithful, I have prepared food for you, and I would like you to honour me by coming to my home along with some distinguished companions. This would strengthen my resolve and also be an honour for me."" 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""We cannot enter your churches with those images in them."""
1255,"It is narrated by Umm Mahajir (may Allah have mercy on her), who said: ""I and some other slave women were brought as captives from Rome. 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) invited us to Islam. So I and one other woman accepted Islam, but no one else did. 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Have these two circumcised and purified.' Then I used to serve 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
1256,"It is narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was circumcised when he was one hundred and twenty years old, and he lived for the remainder of that year. Sa'id (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was the first person to be circumcised, the first to host guests, the first to trim his moustache and clip his nails, and the first whose hair turned white. He said: ""O my Lord, what is this?"" Allah, the Most High, said: ""This is dignity."" Ibrahim (peace be upon him) said: ""O my Lord, increase me in dignity."""
1257,"It is narrated by al-Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him), who said: ""Are you not astonished at Malik ibn Mundhir, who went in search of nine newly converted Muslim farmers in Rome, examined them, and ordered that they be circumcised, even though it was winter (and wounds cause harm)? I came to know that some of them even died. Yet when the Romans and Ethiopians became Muslims during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), no examination was conducted of them (as to whether they had been circumcised or not)."""
1258,"It is narrated by Ibn Shahab al-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him), who said: ""When a person became Muslim, he was commanded to be circumcised, even if he was of advanced age."""
1259,"Ja'far ibn Abi'l-Mughira said, ""Sa'id ibn Jubayr stayed with me
and said tht Ibn 'Abbas related to me that he used to say, 'Where are those
who play with gambling arrows for the slaughtered camel? They buy a camel
with ten shares. Then they shuffle the arrows and it becomes nine shares
and they continue until comes down to one share. The others lose their
shares to the one share. That is gambling (arrow-shuffling).'"""
1260,"Al-Uwaisi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: Al-Maysir is gambling."
1261,"Rabi'a ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Hadir ibn 'Abdullah reported tht two
men wagered two cocks in the time of 'Umar. 'Umar ordered that the cock
be killed and a man of the Ansar said to him, ""Will you kill a something
which glorifies Allah?"" So 'Umar left it."
1262,"Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless
him and grant him peace, said, ""If any of you makes an oath and swears
in his oath by al-Lat and al-'Uzza should say, 'There is no god but Allah.'
If any of you tells him companion, 'Come on, I will make a bet with you'
should give sadaqa."""
1263,"Husayn ibn Mus'ab reported that someone told Abu Hurayra, ""We
wager two pigeons and we do not want for there to be a third unwagered
pigeon between them so that the unwagered pigeon might take the winnings.""
Abu Hurayra said, ""That is how children behave. You are at the point where
you should abandon that."""
